.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-parhel-doctor 1  "parhel 0.2.2" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git\-parhel\-doctor \- Diagnose the environment and clean up after crashed runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit parhel doctor\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-fix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report what would make `add` refuse or misbehave: a source that is not on APFS, staging directories and worktree registrations left by a crashed run, and .git files of other repositories nested in the source. Runs still in progress are detected and never touched.
.PP
With \-\-fix, leftovers are undone using the crashed run\*(Aqs journal: only what that run created is removed, and a worktree that was already published is repaired, not removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<path>\fR [default: .]
Path inside the repository to diagnose
.TP
\fB\-\-fix\fR
Repair leftovers of crashed runs
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
